{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2"],"primary":"c2","title":"Forbidding the Algorithmic Inflation of Rent (FAIR) Act","requirement":"Residential rental property owners may not pay for or subscribe to a coordinator's services, and no person may perform a coordinating function or engage in or facilitate parallel pricing coordination using algorithms that rely on competitors' competitively sensitive information to set or recommend rents, lease terms or occupancy levels. Violations are unlawful under the New Jersey Antitrust Act, and the Attorney General must establish a complaint location and may adopt rules.","key_value":"Ban on use of algorithmic revenue management software or algorithmic devices performing a coordinating function (shared nonpublic data / parallel pricing coordination) for residential rents; effective July 1, 2027","status":"not_yet_effective","effective_date":"2027-07-01","end_date":null,"citation":"P.L.2026, c.43","coverage_conditions":"Applies to all residential dwelling units in New Jersey (houses, apartments, accessory units or other units intended as a primary residence) and to any rental property owner, coordinator or other person. Municipalities may not enact conflicting ordinances, except ordinances explicitly authorized or required by any other law.","exemptions":"Residential dwelling units exclude inpatient medical care, licensed long-term care, and detention or correctional facilities. The following are excluded from 'coordinating function': research, statistical analysis or testing not used to set or recommend terms; free public rent estimates; real estate brokerage databases available on equal terms that do not set or recommend prices or collect sensitive information to do so; and government entities setting or limiting rents through affordability controls. Government entities are not 'coordinators', and parallel pricing required by affordability controls is not covered. Algorithmic devices exclude spreadsheets that do not use AI and require human analysis.","coverage_from":"c2","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
